1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,767
Brief I Q is our pre meeting briefing agent for Global AI Hackathon twenty twenty six, Problem Statement five.

2
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:09,616
It helps users walk into every meeting prepared.

3
00:00:09,616 --> 00:00:13,177
This narrated walkthrough uses screenshots captured from the running application.

4
00:00:14,777 --> 00:00:19,017
Preparing for a meeting often means searching across scattered announcements and news articles.

5
00:00:19,017 --> 00:00:20,975
A summary alone is not enough.

6
00:00:20,975 --> 00:00:26,844
We need to know what changed recently, why it could matter, and where each factual finding came from.

7
00:00:28,444 --> 00:00:35,267
The user chooses a company or public professional, enters the scheduled meeting time and timezone, and can add a meeting purpose.

8
00:00:35,267 --> 00:00:40,789
Brief I Q calculates the preceding thirty days and limits future meeting research to information available now.

9
00:00:42,389 --> 00:00:47,399
Tavily runs focused searches for launches, leadership changes, and other meaningful developments.

10
00:00:47,399 --> 00:00:52,827
The backend filters dates and duplicates, then assembles evidence with stable source identifiers.

11
00:00:52,827 --> 00:00:55,332
Bifrost routes that evidence to Gemini.

12
00:00:55,332 --> 00:01:01,177
Pydantic checks the structured response and citation identifiers before the application renders the briefing.

13
00:01:02,777 --> 00:01:08,243
The result organizes recent context into an executive summary, key developments, and potential implications.

14
00:01:08,243 --> 00:01:11,365
It also suggests discussion points and open questions.

15
00:01:11,365 --> 00:01:13,317
Evidence labels make attribution visible.

16
00:01:13,317 --> 00:01:20,733
The source backed label means the finding cites a retrieved excerpt, so users should still verify the original page.

17
00:01:22,333 --> 00:01:29,200
Each citation opens its source page, and the evidence trail shows retrieved excerpts and publication dates.

18
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,776
Unknown or ambiguous dates remain uncertain.

19
00:01:31,776 --> 00:01:33,921
Unknown citation identifiers cause rejection.

20
00:01:33,921 --> 00:01:40,789
Historical briefings explain verification limits, while future meetings cannot include developments that have not happened yet.

21
00:01:42,389 --> 00:01:45,641
Bifrost is a real part of the inference path.

22
00:01:45,641 --> 00:01:51,061
Every model request goes through the authenticated gateway to Gemini three point five Flash Lite.

23
00:01:51,061 --> 00:01:54,675
The application exposes the requested model and available usage metadata.

24
00:01:54,675 --> 00:01:59,733
Provider credentials stay outside the source code, and no direct provider fallback bypasses Bifrost.

25
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:06,967
Users can download a readable one page PDF, complete Markdown, or copy the briefing text.

26
00:02:06,967 --> 00:02:13,351
If an unusually long report needs more space, the application labels a complete multi page PDF clearly.

27
00:02:13,351 --> 00:02:18,233
It preserves findings, uncertainty notes, and cited links instead of silently cutting content.

28
00:02:19,833 --> 00:02:21,869
Forty eight automated tests pass.

29
00:02:21,869 --> 00:02:27,979
We also verified live Tavily research, Bifrost routed Gemini inference, citation validation, and PDF export.

30
00:02:27,979 --> 00:02:33,680
The project runs locally, with a clearly labeled fictional demo when credentials are unavailable.

31
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:38,567
The full source and setup instructions are in the linked GitHub repository.
